  "flashdocsNeo2Title": "Flash Hibiscus on the Pico Neo 2",
  "flashdocsNeo2Intro": "The full flow on a Linux host: root stock, back it up, then flash the system image.",
  "flashdocsNeo2WarnTitle": "Read this first",
  "flashdocsNeo2WarnBody": "Only the boot and system images below are safe to flash. Writing anything in the bootloader chain below the anti-rollback fuse is a permanent hard-brick on sdm845.",
  "flashdocsNeo2ReqTitle": "Before you start",
  "flashdocsNeo2Req1": "A Linux PC with adb and fastboot",
  "flashdocsNeo2Req2": "A Pico Neo 2 (A7B10) - Eye and non-Eye SKUs both work",
  "flashdocsNeo2Req3": "A USB cable that carries data, not charge-only",
  "flashdocsNeo2RootTitle": "1. Root the headset",
  "flashdocsNeo2RootBody": "Root on stock is what gives the backup step adb root. Download the Magisk-patched boot image, then run:",
  "flashdocsNeo2RootDownload": "Download the patched boot image",
  "flashdocsNeo2RootCmd1": "adb reboot bootloader",
  "flashdocsNeo2RootCmd2": "fastboot oem pico unlock",
  "flashdocsNeo2RootCmd3": "fastboot flash boot magisk_patched_pico_neo_2_boot.img",
  "flashdocsNeo2RootCmd4": "fastboot reboot",
  "flashdocsNeo2RootNote": "oem pico unlock is needed once per fastboot session. If it hangs, power the headset off, boot back into fastboot and run it again.",
  "flashdocsNeo2BackupTitle": "2. Back up stock",
  "flashdocsNeo2BackupBody": "With rooted adb, dump every partition before flashing anything - HBSUP does it end to end, or the tools repo has a backup script if you would rather do it by hand. Keep the dump somewhere safe: it is your only way back to stock.",
  "flashdocsNeo2FlashTitle": "3. Flash Hibiscus",
  "flashdocsNeo2FlashBody": "With the full system image downloaded, put the headset back into fastboot and run:",
  "flashdocsNeo2FlashCmd1": "adb reboot bootloader",
  "flashdocsNeo2FlashCmd2": "fastboot oem pico unlock",
  "flashdocsNeo2FlashCmd3": "fastboot -S 128M flash system system-hibiscus-full.img",
  "flashdocsNeo2FlashCmd4": "fastboot reboot",
  "flashdocsNeo2FlashNote": "The -S 128M chunk size is mandatory: larger chunks kill the USB link mid-flash.",
  "flashdocsNeo2DoneTitle": "4. Done",
  "flashdocsNeo2DoneBody": "The headset restarts into Hibiscus. First boot takes a couple of minutes while the Pico stack settles."
}
